From eaa36b6c644d69812c4967f3aa046d9b9a7a2456 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:20:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire role_matchup, teammate_vacancy (V1 vacancy) and the
 never-built names redzone_tds, role_trend, volume_faced

- role_matchup: "defense ratings conditioned on the player's own ROLE", superseded by the shipped v2_continuous_roles, which gated the
  same branch (a continuous rather than tiered role read on top). The two conditions now read v2_continuous_roles alone.
- teammate_vacancy: the V1 "an OUT teammate's usage redistributed" pass (redistribute_vacated_usage, VACANCY_ABSORB 0.75, VACANCY_MAX_GROWTH
  1.40), superseded by the shipped v2_vacancy (role-specific and ledgered). Removes the function, its three tests and the fallback branch;
  the constants are kept as a comment, the two V2 constants are untouched.
- redzone_tds ("touchdowns from red-zone opportunity", realised later as the shipped v2_xtd), role_trend ("a step change in snap share,
  not a decayed average"; the later share-recency test failed) and volume_faced ("opponent pass/rush volume faced, split"; pace work
  followed) were names with no gating code: registry lines only. The parameter parking lot (docs/weekly_rankings_backlog.md section 4)
  is where such ideas live.
Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
